00:50:24,881 graphrag.callbacks.file_workflow_callbacks INFO Error Invoking LLM details={'input': '\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community\'s key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community\'s name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community\'s overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        "title": <report_title>,\n        "summary": <executive_summary>,\n        "rating": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        "rating_explanation": <rating_explanation>,\n        "findings": [\n            {{\n                "summary":<insight_1_summary>,\n                "explanation": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                "summary":<insight_2_summary>,\n                "explanation": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)]."\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add "+more" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)]."\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    "title": "Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March",\n    "summary": "The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.",\n    "rating": 5.0,\n    "rating_explanation": "The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.",\n    "findings": [\n        {{\n            "summary": "Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location",\n            "explanation": "Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza\'s association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]"\n        }},\n        {{\n            "summary": "Harmony Assembly\'s role in the community",\n            "explanation": "Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]"\n        }},\n        {{\n            "summary": "Unity March as a significant event",\n            "explanation": "The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community\'s dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]"\n        }},\n        {{\n            "summary": "Role of Tribune Spotlight",\n            "explanation": "Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n14983,BURN PATIENTS,"Patients who have suffered burns and are undergoing treatment, often requiring specialized nutritional support",3\r\n4857,KLEK S,"KLEK S is a prominent researcher focused on the field of immunonutrition and its implications for surgical patients. He has contributed significantly to the understanding of how immunonutrition affects malnourished individuals undergoing surgery. In addition to his research, KLEK S is one of the authors of the ESPEN guidelines, which provide comprehensive recommendations for the management of acute intestinal failure. His work is recognized within the clinical nutrition community, particularly in the context of surgery, where he has played a key role in shaping best practices through his involvement with the ESPEN guidelines on clinical nutrition.",8\r\n6741,NUTRITION SUPPORT,"Nutrition support encompasses a range of methods designed to provide nutritional intake to patients who are unable to eat normally due to various medical conditions. This includes enteral feeding, which delivers nutrients directly to the gastrointestinal tract, and parenteral feeding, which provides nutrients intravenously. It is particularly crucial for managing conditions such as acute pancreatitis, where patients may struggle to absorb food effectively. \n\nNutrition support is essential in critical care settings and is especially important for hospitalized pediatric patients, including those with obesity or other health issues. The primary goal of nutrition support is to ensure that patients receive adequate nutrients to meet their needs when they cannot do so through regular eating. Overall, nutrition support plays a vital role in the recovery and management of patients with significant health challenges.",7\r\n4853,BRAGA M,"Braga M is a prominent researcher and author known for significant contributions to the field of surgical nutrition. He has focused on enhanced recovery after surgery and the impact of immunonutrition on surgical outcomes. As an expert in this area, Braga M is associated with the ESPEN guidelines, specifically those pertaining to clinical nutrition in surgery and parenteral nutrition related to surgical practices. Additionally, he has played a vital role in formulating consensus recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit, further establishing his influence and expertise in the field of surgical nutrition.",8\r\n12941,IMMUNONUTRITION,"Immunonutrition is a specialized nutritional approach designed to enhance the immune response, particularly in patients undergoing surgery for cancer, those suffering from trauma, and critically ill individuals. This field of study focuses on the effects of specific nutrients on the immune system, aiming to improve outcomes for patients in critical conditions. By implementing targeted nutritional strategies, immunonutrition seeks to bolster the immune system\'s effectiveness, thereby supporting recovery and overall health in vulnerable populations.",11\r\n14984,CANCER SURGERY,"Surgical procedures performed on patients with cancer, which may require immunomodulatory nutritional formulas",2\r\n13613,NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT IN ONCOLOGY,Nutritional support in oncology refers to the assessment and management of nutritional needs for cancer patients to improve their health outcomes.,2\r\n6740,PANCREATICODUODENECTOMY,"Pancreaticoduodenectomy, commonly referred to as the Whipple procedure, is a complex surgical operation that involves the removal of the head of the pancreas, part of the small intestine (duodenum), and other nearby structures. This procedure is primarily performed on patients diagnosed with pancreatic cancer. Due to the extensive nature of the surgery, patients often require specialized nutritional support during their recovery.",5\r\n14985,TRIALS,Clinical trials conducted to evaluate the effectiveness of various nutritional formulas in patients with specific medical conditions,1\r\n4729,ANNALS OF SURGERY,"The ""ANNALS OF SURGERY"" is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research related to surgical practices and outcomes. It features a variety of articles, including meta-analyses concerning immunonutrition in surgery and studies that estimate mortality risk in preoperative patients. Additionally, the journal includes research on specific surgical conditions, such as medullary thyroid cancer. Through its comprehensive coverage of surgical topics, the ""ANNALS OF SURGERY"" serves as a significant resource for medical professionals in the field of surgery.",3\r\n12927,JPEN JOURNAL OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION,"The JPEN Journal of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition is a scholarly journal dedicated to publishing research focused on nutrition support within clinical settings. It specifically addresses practices and protocols related to both parenteral and enteral nutrition, providing a platform for the dissemination of knowledge and advancements in the field of nutritional support.",4\r\n13561,ARCHIVES OF IMMUNOLOGY AND THERAPY EXPERIMENTAL,"A journal that publishes research on immunology and its applications in therapy, including studies on immunonutrition in cancer patients.",1\r\n13560,EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF SURGICAL ONCOLOGY,"A journal that publishes research on surgical oncology, including studies on the efficacy of immunonutrition in cancer surgeries.",1\r\n13562,CLINICAL SCIENCE,"A journal that publishes research on clinical and experimental medicine, including studies on the effects of immunonutrition in cancer patients.",1\r\n12946,CRITICAL ILLNESS,,2\r\n13558,SURGICAL ONCOLOGY,"A journal focused on the field of surgical oncology, publishing studies on cancer treatment and outcomes, including immunonutrition.",1\r\n13559,NUTRITION AND CANCER,"A journal that explores the relationship between nutrition and cancer, including studies on immunonutrition and its effects on cancer patients.",1\r\n13694,CHRISTOU NV,"Christou NV is an organization involved in medical research, particularly in estimating mortality risk in preoperative patients.",3\r\n12931,IBRAHIM EH,Ibrahim EH is a researcher who studied the effects of early versus late enteral feeding in mechanically ventilated patients.,1\r\n12934,KOZAR RA,Kozar RA is a researcher who studied enteral tolerance post-injury through standardized protocols.,1\r\n14988,CENTRAL EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF IMMUNOLOGY,,1\r\n13696,CHARTRAND L,Chartrand L is a researcher involved in the study of mortality risk in preoperative patients.,1\r\n13695,TELLADO RODRIGUEZ J,Tellado Rodríguez J is a researcher contributing to studies on mortality risk in preoperative patients.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3808,NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT,BURN PATIENTS,Nutritional support is critical for burn patients to aid in their recovery,136\r\n2929,ESPEN,KLEK S,Klek S contribuyó a las guías de ESPEN sobre la gestión de la falla intestinal aguda,93\r\n2951,ESPEN,NUTRITION SUPPORT,ESPEN provides guidelines for nutrition support in patients with conditions like pancreatitis,92\r\n7991,PANCREATITIS,NUTRITION SUPPORT,Nutrition support is essential for patients with pancreatitis to ensure proper recovery,63\r\n9772,HYPE