overy After Surgery (ERAS) programs, which aim to reduce costs and length of stay.",5\r\n12583,ENHANCED RECOVERY AFTER SURGERY,Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) is a program established to improve recovery for patients undergoing elective surgery through multimodal rehabilitation protocols.,16\r\n12586,NORWAY,"Norway is a significant contributor to international health and research initiatives. It provided data for the World Health Organization\'s (WHO) international growth reference patterns for children, aiding in the establishment of global health standards. Additionally, Norway is one of the five northern European countries that played a crucial role in the formation of the Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) group, which focuses on improving surgical recovery protocols. Through these contributions, Norway demonstrates its commitment to advancing health and medical practices on an international scale.",2\r\n12592,RECTAL SURGERY,"Rectal surgery encompasses surgical procedures performed on the rectum, which may incorporate Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols to enhance patient outcomes. These protocols are designed to optimize recovery and improve overall surgical results, making rectal surgery a critical component of modern surgical practices.",2\r\n12593,MORBIDITY,"Morbidity refers to the condition of being diseased or the incidence of illness, encompassing the presence of disease or medical conditions that affect health and quality of life. It is a critical focus for initiatives like Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS), which aims to reduce morbidity through improved surgical protocols.",2\r\n12584,KEHLET,Kehlet is a medical professional who proposed new strategies for perioperative management to reduce surgical stress and improve recovery in 1997.,1\r\n12585,SCOTLAND,Scotland is one of the five northern European countries that contributed to the establishment of the ERAS group.,1\r\n12587,NETHERLANDS,The Netherlands is one of the five northern European countries that contributed to the establishment of the ERAS group.,1\r\n12588,MULTIMODAL REHABILITATION,Multimodal rehabilitation refers to the combination of various interventions aimed at improving recovery outcomes for patients undergoing surgery.,1\r\n12589,PERIOPERATIVE CARE,"Perioperative care encompasses the care provided before, during, and after surgery, which is crucial for patient recovery.",1\r\n12590,FAST-TRACK SURGERY,Fast-track surgery is a term used to describe surgical protocols designed to expedite recovery and reduce hospital stay.,1\r\n12602,COLON SURGERY,,1\r\n8022,COSTS OF CARE,"Costs of care refer to the financial implications associated with treating patients, which can be influenced by their nutritional status.",1\r\n12598,MULTIDISCIPLINARY INTEGRATION,"Multidisciplinary integration involves collaboration among various healthcare professionals, which is essential for the successful implementation of ERAS protocols.",1\r\n13615,RISK FACTORS,Risk factors are characteristics or conditions that increase the likelihood of developing a disease or injury.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n2789,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ERAS,Las recomendaciones de ERAS incluyen el uso de nutrición enteral para mejorar la recuperación postoperatoria,340\r\n3755,NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT,ERAS,Nutritional support is a key component of the ERAS protocol aimed at improving surgical outcomes.,138\r\n2360,PATIENT,HOSPITALIZATION,The patient was hospitalized for medical care and nutritional support,129\r\n15392,BARIATRIC SURGERY,ENHANCED RECOVERY AFTER SURGERY,Bariatric surgery is included in the Enhanced Recovery After Surgery protocols to improve recovery outcomes,88\r\n6418,NUTRITION,ENHANCED RECOVERY AFTER SURGERY,Nutrition is a key focus area in the Enhanced Recovery After Surgery program to support patient recovery,71\r\n5965,OMS,NORWAY,Norway was part of the data collection for the WHO\'s international